  "eligible_design": true,
  "eligible_reason": "Staggered binary treatment: a book title becomes 'banned' in the month of its first ban event (months_since_first_ban = 0, post_ban = 1 from then on), with first-ban months differing across titles (seven distinct first-ban months among the 22 banned titles in gr_reviews_data.csv; the library circulation analysis uses the same title-level event timing) and a large set of never-banned control titles (is_control_title). Main-text Tables 3-7 estimate linear TWFE regressions of log circulation on post_ban x is_banned_ever with title and calendar-month fixed effects (plus state FE in the state-title-month library panel), clustered by state, in a -4/+6 month window, with no covariates; Table 5 reports Callaway-Sant'Anna (att_gt, not-yet-treated controls), Sun-Abraham (sunab) and Borusyak-Jaravel-Spiess (did_imputation) aggregates alongside TWFE; Figures 4-7 and 9 are unstacked event studies (i(months_since_first_ban, is_banned_ever, -1)). Ineligible columns: ban-intensity interactions (Table 3 col 4), heterogeneity triple interactions (Table 4 cols 4-5, Table 6 col 2), single-date 'complete spillover'/alternate identification columns (Table 5 col 5, Table 7 col 4), PSM-matched controls (Table 6 col 8). Caveat on FE: the library panel is state x title x month but the FE are state + title + running_month (title is the assignment unit, state an additional additive FE); the authors' own CSA/BJS use state-title as the unit id with title-level cohorts.",
  "design_notes": "R code (fixest, did, didimputation). Main data lib_circ_data.csv: state-title-month library circulation (ln_circ) for banned titles (is_banned_title; top-25 most-banned = is_top_25_title) and control titles; sample window months_since_first_ban in [-4, 6]; post_ban = as.integer(months_since_first_ban >= 0); controls have post_ban = 0 throughout (confirmed in gr_reviews_data.csv where control rows all have post_ban 0 and months_since_first_ban -1), so post_ban*is_banned_ever reduces to the interaction. CSA: att_gt(yname ln_circ, tname running_month, idname id = state_title index, gname ban_group = title's first-ban month, xformla ~1, control_group notyettreated, allow_unbalanced_panel) on cs_did_data.csv; aggte simple. SA: sunab(month_treated, running_month, ref.p = -1), agg ATT. BJS: did_imputation(gname ban_group, tname running_month, idname id). Table 7 uses Seattle Public Library title-month data (spl_circ_data.csv, Title + month FE, heteroskedastic SEs). Table 8 uses candidate-month small-dollar donations with cand_state + CAND_ID + month + cand_state^month FE, treatment post_ban (state's first ban month) x is_rep_cmt. Appendix Table A6 (Goodreads reviews, title-month, title + running_month FE) is the only part replicable from the shipped data.",
  "estimators_reported": ["twfe_static", "twfe_event_study", "callaway_santanna", "sun_abraham", "borusyak_jaravel_spiess", "twfe_static_weighted"],
  "main_or_robustness": "main",
